<DocsLayout title="batze docs — Client email" description="Connect a mailbox and keep client conversations next to the work they belong to.">
  <h1>Client email</h1>
  <p>Read and reply to client email without leaving batze — every message filed against the project it belongs to.</p>

  <h2 id="connect">Connecting a mailbox</h2>
  <p>
    Point batze at your mailbox over IMAP/SMTP and set <code>SMTP_URL</code> in your
    <a href="/docs/configuration">configuration</a>. From then on, mail you send and receive shows up in batze.
  </p>

  <h2 id="linked">Linked to projects</h2>
  <p>Messages are matched to the right client and project, so the conversation always sits next to the work it's about.</p>

  <h2 id="templates">Templates</h2>
  <p>Save the replies you send again and again as templates, and drop them in with a click.</p>
</DocsLayout>
